doc:
The Frobenius norm is continuous on finite matrix arrays.
Source: finite sums, products, and the continuous square root;
atlas norm-lipschitz (cutoff helper).

A coordinate pinch keeps the diagonal and the untouched block, and kills
the other entries in its row and column. Bhatia 1997, IX.3;
atlas `golden-thompson` (entrywise pinching formula).

Each actual coordinate derivative equals the corresponding entry of
the explicit resolvent Gram gradient. Source: operator tail proof;
atlas `wishart-lambda-min-tail` (helper).

